{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtRegularMultiplicity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtRegularMultiplicity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtBlockDimension"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtRegularMultiplicity.finrank_homG_regular_partitionIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtRegularMultiplicity.finrank_homG_regular_partitionIndex","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtRegularMultiplicity.lean#L62-L66","doc":"The same statement indexed by `PartitionIndex n`, the form the block count consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtRegularMultiplicity.finrank_homG_regular_specht","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtRegularMultiplicity.finrank_homG_regular_specht","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtRegularMultiplicity.lean#L46-L59","doc":"**The multiplicity of `S^μ` in the regular representation is `dim_k S^μ`.**\n\nImmediate from `RegularHom.finrank_homG_regular` once the Specht module is viewed as a\nrepresentation of `Perm (Fin n)`. It is stated separately because `Hom_G(k[G], −)` is only a\n*multiplicity* space because the commutant is the base field, which is W2\n(`SpechtAbsolutelyIrreducible.specht_end_scalar`, via the orthonormality of\n`SpechtSchurDiagonal.finrank_homG_specht`); over a base where the commutant were a larger\ndivision ring this dimension would count multiplicity in units of `dim 𝔇`, not on the nose.\n\n`-- Ref: [sagan2001] §1.10`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}